---
title: Leek, Carrot and Potato Pie
author: Shirley Simmonds
servings: 3
cook time: 1 hour
---

Preheat the oven to 180°C.

Bring a #saucepan{} of salted @water{} to boiling point, then put in @potatoes{450%g} and @carrots{225%g}; bring them to the boil, cover and cook for about ~{15%minutes}. Then drain them, reserving the water.

Now return the pan you cooked them in to the heat and melt @butter{50%g} in it. Add the washed, drained @leeks{450%g}(halved lengthways and cut into 5mm-thick slices) and @onion{1}(peeled and chopped), and cook them gently for about ~{6%minutes}, or until softened.

Now slice the potatoes and carrots thinly and arrange them in layers in a well-buttered baking dish. Season, then add the leeks and onion.

Make up the @white sauce{275%ml}(made with @butter{40%g}, @plain flour{20%g}, @milk{150%ml}(semi-skimmed) and @vegetable stock{150%ml}, a pinch of @ground mace{}), and pour it over the vegetables. Scatter @Cheddar cheese{75%g}(grated), @fresh white breadcrumbs{1%tbsp}, and a couple of pinches of @cayenne pepper{} on the top, and bake for about ~{1%hour}.
